TASK SPECIFICATIONS:
{
  "id": "PUB013",
  "title": "Office HVAC Multi-mode Energy-Saving Control",
  "difficulty": "medium",
  "requirements": "# Office HVAC Multi-mode Energy-Saving Control\n\n- **Difficulty:** Medium (medium)\n\n## Requirements\n\nControl an office-building supply fan and generate a temperature-setpoint adjustment from occupancy, operating mode and the energy-saving selection.\n\n1. Valid HVAC_MODE_SELECTOR values are 0 (Auto), 1 (Comfort), 2 (Economy) and 3 (Night).\n2. Start a 30-second delay only when occupancy is detected and Night mode is not selected. SUPPLY_FAN_RUN becomes TRUE only after these conditions remain satisfied for 30 seconds. Immediately stop the fan and reset timing if occupancy is lost or Night mode is selected. Wait the full 30 seconds again when the conditions recover.\n3. Auto mode: use a 0\u00b0C adjustment when occupied. When unoccupied, use +3\u00b0C in energy-saving mode or +2\u00b0C in standard mode.\n4. Comfort mode: use 0\u00b0C when occupied or +1\u00b0C when unoccupied. Economy mode: use 0\u00b0C when occupied or +4\u00b0C when unoccupied.\n5. Night mode: use +4\u00b0C regardless of occupancy. The energy-saving selection affects only Auto mode.\n6. Keep TEMP_SETPOINT_ADJUST within \u00b14\u00b0C. Initialize outputs to OFF and zero at power-up; update them from current inputs when normal calculation begins.\n7. The start delay controls only the BOOL fan enable; no continuous speed ramp is required.\n\n## Interface Definition\n\n| Direction | Variable/Field | Data Type | Description |\n| --- | --- | --- | --- |\n| Input | `OCCUPANCY_DETECTED` | `BOOL` | Occupancy-detection result derived from the CO\u2082 sensor. |\n| Input | `ENERGY_SAVING_MODE` | `BOOL` | TRUE selects energy saving; FALSE selects standard operation; affects Auto mode only. |\n| Input | `HVAC_MODE_SELECTOR` | `INT` | 0 Auto, 1 Comfort, 2 Economy, 3 Night; callers supply a valid value. |\n| Output | `SUPPLY_FAN_RUN` | `BOOL` | Supply-fan run enable. |\n| Output | `TEMP_SETPOINT_ADJUST` | `INT` | Temperature-setpoint adjustment in \u00b0C. |",
  "scenario": "An office fan uses a restartable occupancy delay and mode-dependent temperature setback.",
  "interface": [
    {
      "direction": "INPUT",
      "name": "OCCUPANCY_DETECTED",
      "type": "BOOL",
      "description": "Occupancy-detection result derived from the CO\u2082 sensor."
    },
    {
      "direction": "INPUT",
      "name": "ENERGY_SAVING_MODE",
      "type": "BOOL",
      "description": "TRUE selects energy saving; FALSE selects standard operation; affects Auto mode only."
    },
    {
      "direction": "INPUT",
      "name": "HVAC_MODE_SELECTOR",
      "type": "INT",
      "description": "0 Auto, 1 Comfort, 2 Economy, 3 Night; callers supply a valid value."
    },
    {
      "direction": "OUTPUT",
      "name": "SUPPLY_FAN_RUN",
      "type": "BOOL",
      "description": "Supply-fan run enable."
    },
    {
      "direction": "OUTPUT",
      "name": "TEMP_SETPOINT_ADJUST",
      "type": "INT",
      "description": "Temperature-setpoint adjustment in \u00b0C."
    }
  ],
  "initial_conditions": {
    "SUPPLY_FAN_RUN": false,
    "TEMP_SETPOINT_ADJUST": 0
  },
  "scan_semantics": "Inputs I[k] are sampled at invocation; outputs O[k] are observed after the call. Retained pre-state q[k] becomes q[k+1]. Each test resets the instance. A transition affects the same observed scan. dt_ms is elapsed time since the preceding invocation; the first invocation starts IEC timers at elapsed zero. CycleTime inputs, where supplied, are attributed to the current invocation rather than inferred from dt_ms.",
  "safety_priority": [
    "Occupancy loss or Night immediately stops fan and resets delay.",
    "Energy saving affects only Auto setback."
  ],
  "assumptions": [
    "Selector values are always 0..3 as required by the official input contract.",
    "Outputs are initialized before the first call, which calculates adjustment immediately.",
    "The timer starts at elapsed zero on the first non-Night occupied call. Fan starts at the first observation at or after 30s.",
    "dt_ms is actual elapsed time since the preceding call; real runtime timer tests must preserve this timing.",
    "The task interface, requirements, assumptions, and normalized LTL definitions (excluding reference-only ground truth) are supplied identically to both frameworks. Output names always denote observed candidate outputs, never precomputed expected values.",
    "The task interface, requirements, assumptions, and normalized LTL definitions (excluding reference-only ground truth) are supplied identically to both frameworks. Output names always denote observed candidate outputs, never precomputed expected values."
  ],
  "atomic_propositions": {
    "permit": "OCCUPANCY_DETECTED AND HVAC_MODE_SELECTOR<>3",
    "mature": "continuous permit elapsed>=30s",
    "fan": "SUPPLY_FAN_RUN",
    "bounded": "-4<=TEMP_SETPOINT_ADJUST<=4",
    "occupied": "OCCUPANCY_DETECTED AND mode<>3",
    "zero": "TEMP_SETPOINT_ADJUST=0",
    "night": "mode=3",
    "four": "adjust=4",
    "auto_save": "mode=0 AND NOT occupancy AND ENERGY_SAVING_MODE",
    "three": "adjust=3",
    "auto_standard": "mode=0 AND NOT occupancy AND NOT ENERGY_SAVING_MODE",
    "two": "adjust=2",
    "comfort": "mode=1 AND NOT occupancy",
    "one": "adjust=1",
    "economy": "mode=2 AND NOT occupancy",
    "TimeTick": "Boolean: floor(t[k]/1ms)>floor(t[k-1]/1ms), with t[0]=0, TimeTick[0]=FALSE, t[k]=sum(dt_ms[1..k]). G(F(TimeTick)) states unbounded physical time progress; merely positive dt is insufficient.",
    "OCCUPANCY_DETECTED": "I[k].OCCUPANCY_DETECTED: sampled input (BOOL).",
    "ENERGY_SAVING_MODE": "I[k].ENERGY_SAVING_MODE: sampled input (BOOL).",
    "HVAC_MODE_SELECTOR": "I[k].HVAC_MODE_SELECTOR: sampled input (INT).",
    "SUPPLY_FAN_RUN": "O[k].SUPPLY_FAN_RUN: independently observed post-scan candidate value (BOOL); never defined as expected output.",
    "TEMP_SETPOINT_ADJUST": "O[k].TEMP_SETPOINT_ADJUST: independently observed post-scan candidate value (INT); never defined as expected output.",
    "mode": "I[k].HVAC_MODE_SELECTOR",
    "occupancy": "I[k].OCCUPANCY_DETECTED",
    "adjust": "O[k].TEMP_SETPOINT_ADJUST",
    "init": "At the separate pre-invocation initial observation before scan k=0: O_init.SUPPLY_FAN_RUN=false, O_init.TEMP_SETPOINT_ADJUST=0."
  },
  "ltl": [
    {
      "id": "PUB013.P_init",
      "kind": "safety",
      "formula": "init",
      "description": "Before the first scan invocation, all declared OUTPUT variables and initial instance state hold their declared initial values.",
      "explanation": "Applies strictly to the fresh pre-invocation initial instance observation before scan k=0 (INITIAL_INSTANCE scope).",
      "language": "LTL_OVER_TYPED_SCAN_PREDICATES",
      "encoding_status": "NOT_LOWERED_TO_MODEL_CHECKER",
      "scope": "INITIAL_INSTANCE"
    },
    {
      "id": "PUB013.P1",
      "name": "Fan delay",
      "formula": "G(fan <-> (permit & mature))",
      "explanation": "Fan follows the complete uninterrupted delay.",
      "language": "LTL_OVER_TYPED_SCAN_PREDICATES",
      "encoding_status": "NOT_LOWERED_TO_MODEL_CHECKER",
      "scope": "SCAN_SEQUENCE"
    },
    {
      "id": "PUB013.P2",
      "name": "Bounds",
      "formula": "G(bounded)",
      "explanation": "Legal outputs satisfy the required range.",
      "language": "LTL_OVER_TYPED_SCAN_PREDICATES",
      "encoding_status": "NOT_LOWERED_TO_MODEL_CHECKER",
      "scope": "SCAN_SEQUENCE"
    },
    {
      "id": "PUB013.P3",
      "name": "Occupied and Night",
      "formula": "G((occupied -> zero) & (night -> four))",
      "explanation": "Night overrides occupied setback.",
      "language": "LTL_OVER_TYPED_SCAN_PREDICATES",
      "encoding_status": "NOT_LOWERED_TO_MODEL_CHECKER",
      "scope": "SCAN_SEQUENCE"
    },
    {
      "id": "PUB013.P4",
      "name": "Auto",
      "formula": "G((auto_save -> three) & (auto_standard -> two))",
      "explanation": "Auto unoccupied setback follows energy saving.",
      "language": "LTL_OVER_TYPED_SCAN_PREDICATES",
      "encoding_status": "NOT_LOWERED_TO_MODEL_CHECKER",
      "scope": "SCAN_SEQUENCE"
    },
    {
      "id": "PUB013.P5",
      "name": "Fixed modes",
      "formula": "G((comfort -> one) & (economy -> four))",
      "explanation": "Comfort and Economy ignore energy saving.",
      "language": "LTL_OVER_TYPED_SCAN_PREDICATES",
      "encoding_status": "NOT_LOWERED_TO_MODEL_CHECKER",
      "scope": "SCAN_SEQUENCE"
    },
    {
      "id": "PUB013.P6",
      "name": "Liveness",
      "formula": "(G(F(TimeTick))) -> (G((G permit) -> F fan))",
      "explanation": "If permit stays TRUE from any scan onward, the fan eventually runs, assuming continued calls and diverging physical time. Explicit non-Zeno environment premise: physical elapsed time crosses infinitely many 1ms boundaries.",
      "language": "LTL_OVER_TYPED_SCAN_PREDICATES",
      "encoding_status": "NOT_LOWERED_TO_MODEL_CHECKER",
      "scope": "SCAN_SEQUENCE"
    }
  ]
}

ARCHITECTURAL PLAN:
{
  "state_machine": [
    {
      "state": "BLOCKED",
      "meaning": "Occupancy is absent or Night is selected; fan is off and the delay is reset.",
      "transitions": [
        {
          "condition": "OCCUPANCY_DETECTED AND HVAC_MODE_SELECTOR <> 3",
          "to": "PERMITTED"
        },
        {
          "condition": "NOT OCCUPANCY_DETECTED OR HVAC_MODE_SELECTOR = 3",
          "to": "BLOCKED"
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "state": "PERMITTED",
      "meaning": "The fan is waiting while the timer Q is false and running while Q is true.",
      "transitions": [
        {
          "condition": "NOT OCCUPANCY_DETECTED OR HVAC_MODE_SELECTOR = 3",
          "to": "BLOCKED"
        },
        {
          "condition": "OCCUPANCY_DETECTED AND HVAC_MODE_SELECTOR <> 3",
          "to": "PERMITTED"
        }
      ]
    }
  ],
  "timer_plan": [
    {
      "name": "FAN_START_DELAY",
      "type": "IEC TON",
      "PT": "T#30s",
      "input": "OCCUPANCY_DETECTED AND HVAC_MODE_SELECTOR <> 3",
      "reset_conditions": "Call with IN = FALSE on occupancy loss or selection of Night; initialize the instance reset at power-up.",
      "timing": "The first permitted call starts at elapsed zero. Q becomes true on the first call at or after 30 seconds of continuously sampled permit. Switching among Auto, Comfort and Economy does not reset the timer."
    }
  ],
  "priorities": [
    "Occupancy loss or Night stops the fan and resets the timer in the same observed scan.",
    "Night temperature adjustment overrides occupancy and energy-saving selection.",
    "Energy-saving selection affects only unoccupied Auto adjustment.",
    "Temperature adjustment is independent of the fan delay and is bounded to -4 through +4 degrees Celsius."
  ],
  "initial_values": {
    "scope": "Fresh instance, before the first invocation",
    "SUPPLY_FAN_RUN": false,
    "TEMP_SETPOINT_ADJUST": 0,
    "state": "BLOCKED",
    "previous_permit": false,
    "FAN_START_DELAY.Q": false,
    "FAN_START_DELAY.ET": "T#0s"
  },
  "scan_execution_order": [
    {
      "stage": 1,
      "name": "Edge sampling",
      "action": "Snapshot all inputs. Compute permit as OCCUPANCY_DETECTED AND HVAC_MODE_SELECTOR <> 3. Derive rising and falling permit edges from previous_permit, then update previous_permit. Edges are observational; timer control uses the permit level."
    },
    {
      "stage": 2,
      "name": "Safety/reset priority and state transitions",
      "action": "If permit is false, select BLOCKED; otherwise select PERMITTED. This transition takes effect in the current scan. Do not use a previous-scan timer Q to decide the fan output."
    },
    {
      "stage": 3,
      "name": "Unconditional top-level timer FB calls outside CASE/IF",
      "action": "Call FAN_START_DELAY exactly once with IN := permit and PT := T#30s. Its current-call Q and reset are available to stage 4."
    },
    {
      "stage": 4,
      "name": "Unified output assignments",
      "action": "Assign SUPPLY_FAN_RUN := permit AND FAN_START_DELAY.Q. Calculate TEMP_SETPOINT_ADJUST from the sampled inputs: Night = 4; otherwise occupied = 0; otherwise Auto = 3 if energy saving is true or 2 if false, Comfort = 1, Economy = 4. Clamp the result to [-4, 4]. Calculate outputs on the first invocation as well."
    }
  ],
  "formal_assertions": [
    {
      "id": "A1",
      "formula": "G(SUPPLY_FAN_RUN -> (OCCUPANCY_DETECTED AND HVAC_MODE_SELECTOR <> 3))"
    },
    {
      "id": "A2",
      "formula": "G(TEMP_SETPOINT_ADJUST >= -4 AND TEMP_SETPOINT_ADJUST <= 4)"
    },
    {
      "id": "A3",
      "formula": "G((HVAC_MODE_SELECTOR = 3) -> (TEMP_SETPOINT_ADJUST = 4))"
    },
    {
      "id": "A4",
      "formula": "G((OCCUPANCY_DETECTED AND HVAC_MODE_SELECTOR <> 3) -> (TEMP_SETPOINT_ADJUST = 0))"
    },
    {
      "id": "A5",
      "formula": "G((HVAC_MODE_SELECTOR = 0 AND NOT OCCUPANCY_DETECTED AND ENERGY_SAVING_MODE) -> (TEMP_SETPOINT_ADJUST = 3))"
    },
    {
      "id": "A6",
      "formula": "G((HVAC_MODE_SELECTOR = 0 AND NOT OCCUPANCY_DETECTED AND NOT ENERGY_SAVING_MODE) -> (TEMP_SETPOINT_ADJUST = 2))"
    },
    {
      "id": "A7",
      "formula": "G((HVAC_MODE_SELECTOR = 1 AND NOT OCCUPANCY_DETECTED) -> (TEMP_SETPOINT_ADJUST = 1))"
    },
    {
      "id": "A8",
      "formula": "G((HVAC_MODE_SELECTOR = 2 AND NOT OCCUPANCY_DETECTED) -> (TEMP_SETPOINT_ADJUST = 4))"
    }
  ]
}

CODESYS DIALECT CARDS:
[
  {
    "id": "ton_timer",
    "title": "Standard IEC TON Timer Block Invocation",
    "body": "// Standard IEC TON timer: MUST invoke unconditionally OUTSIDE CASE/IF every scan!\nVAR\n    timer : TON;\n    runTimer : BOOL;\nEND_VAR\n// Control via boolean IN flag (never put timer(...) only inside an IF/CASE arm):\nrunTimer := (state = 1) AND NOT resetCmd;\ntimer(IN := runTimer, PT := T#2s);\nIF timer.Q THEN\n    // Timer expired; timer.ET holds elapsed time\nEND_IF;"
  },
  {
    "id": "case_state_machine",
    "title": "Explicit CASE State Machine Transitions",
    "body": "// 4-Stage Scan Order: 1) Edge sample 2) Reset/priority & CASE state transition\n// 3) Unconditional top-level TON/R_TRIG calls 4) Unified output assignments\nVAR\n    state : INT := 0; // 0=IDLE, 1=RUN, 2=FAULT\nEND_VAR\nIF emergencyStop THEN state := 2; END_IF;\nCASE state OF\n    0: IF startCmd AND NOT fault THEN state := 1; END_IF;\n    1: IF faultCmd THEN state := 2; ELSIF stopCmd THEN state := 0; END_IF;\n    2: IF resetCmd THEN state := 0; END_IF;\n    ELSE state := 0;\nEND_CASE;\noutActive := (state = 1); // Assign outputs unconditionally from current state"
  }
]
